<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keryneia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ceryneia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keryneia, or Ceryneia, was an ancient town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, in the hills south of Helike. Pausanias records that refugees from Mycenae settled there after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> destroyed their city in the 5th century BCE. In the 270s BCE its tyrant Iseas resigned and the town joined the refounded Achaean League, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margus-of-keryneia">Margus of Keryneia</a> became the league's first sole general in 255 BCE.</p></div>
